ention and Policy Title IX and Sexual Assault Workplace Violence Policy 7C Demonstration Policy Annual Fire Safety and Security Report About Toggle Dropdown Visit Campus Harvey Mudd  News Upcoming Events Fast Facts History President's Office Mission and Strategic Planning Giving Toggle Dropdown Make Your Gift Now Annual Fund Endowed Giving at Harvey Mudd Planned Giving Current and Special Giving Initiatives Ways to Give Contact College Advancement Close Submit Faculty Positions Home Dean of the Faculty Faculty Positions Adjunct Professors of Engineering DOF Menu Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Academic Affairs Toggle sub-menu of Academic Affairs Exam Schedules Academic Affairs for Incoming Students Academic Affairs for Current Students Faculty Positions Faculty Development at Harvey Mudd College Toggle sub-menu of Faculty Development at Harvey Mudd College Faculty Development through NCFDD Faculty Policies and Procedures Faculty Mentoring Council of Undergraduate Research Resources for Early-Career Faculty Internal Items See Also Faculty Research Resources Honor Code Resources Innovation Accelerator (IA) Grants – Guidelines and Procedures webpage Adjunct Professors of Engineering September 28, 2026 Harvey Mudd College invites applications for Adjunct Professors of Engineering for our general engineering program for the Spring 2026 semester (January – May). The Department of Engineering seeks candidates with experience and knowledge in applications of engineering who can excel at teaching in a broadly-based undergraduate curriculum focused on design, systems engineering, and engineering science. Applicants must have a demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and professional growth. The candidate must have completed or be close to completing a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in engineering or a related field.  Industrial or other practical experience in the field is valued. Each adjunct will teach one (or optionally more) of the following classes: E83 (Continuum Mechanics), E84 (Electronic and Magnetic Circuits and Devices) or engineering elective courses negotiated at the time of hire.  E83 and E84 are required core courses (sophomore/junior level) and reference teaching materials are available.  Engineering electives are junior/senior level courses and may be adapted to the instructor’s particular expertise. All registered classes taught during the academic year must be taught in person and on campus, in line with the HMC Academic Catalog and HMC Faculty Notebook. Applicants should submit: a cover letter, a curriculum vitæ, and the names of at least three references. Candidates should provide evidence of excellence in teaching. For full consideration, applications should be received by October 26, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. The Engineering Department at Harvey Mudd College strives to embody the values of equity and inclusion through the work and community of our students, staff and faculty. Harvey Mudd College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Qualified applicants will be given consideration for employment without regard to age, race, gender, national origin, sexual orientation, protected veteran’s status, disability, or any other status protected by applicable law. https://www.hmc.edu/human-resources/policies-procedures-and-guidelines/equal-opportunity-and-nondiscrimination-statement/ Any questions may be sent to engadjprofspr27-l@g.hmc.edu https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32857 Posts navigation Previous post Browse by Category Select category… Uncategorized Go Browse by Date Select month... September 2026 August 2026 Go Employment Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Harvey Mudd College is an equal opportunity employer committed to providing a workplace free of discrimination, harassment, and disrespectful or other unprofessional conduct. Employment Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Statement . Request Info Visit Apply 301 Platt Blvd., Claremont, CA 91711 909.621.8000 | info@hmc.edu Your support helps educate compassionate leaders in STEM. Give now » The official store for Harvey Mudd College apparel and merchandise Shop HMC » Safety Information Immigration Resources & Information Mudders Care for Mudders Map and Directions Directory Privacy Statement Accessibility Equal Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Statement Employment at Harvey Mudd Harvey Mudd College does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of any status or condition protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. © Copyright 2026 | Harvey Mudd College is a member of The Claremont Colleges Harvey Mudd College Official Facebook Harvey Mudd College Official Instagram Harvey Mudd College Official BlueSky Harvey Mudd College Official YouTube Harvey Mudd College Official Flickr Harvey Mudd College Official LinkedIn"
